   "html_text": "In one of the authors’ studies, participants were asked to imagine that they had signed a contract, and that the contract either came into effect immediately and could be nullified anytime in the first 72 hours, or that the contract would come into effect after 72 hours unless it was nullified before then. Participants reported being more open to shopping around for a better alternative in the second condition (in which the contract was not in effect) than in the first (in which it was)—even tho",
